<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria II of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819–1853</span> · Also known as Maria da Glória</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria II was Queen of Portugal from 1826 to 1828 and from 1834 to 1853. Daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Pedro I of Brazil</a>, she became queen when her father abdicated the Portuguese throne, but her uncle Miguel usurped it in 1828. Pedro's liberal forces won the civil war of 1828 to 1834 and restored her, and she reigned as a constitutional monarch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-ii-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Maria II of Portugal" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Simpson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_D._Maria_II,_Queen_of_Portugal_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
